course: dictionary
lesson: 7748
title: Punctuation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Punctuation is the set of small marks that make writing clear: full stops, commas, question marks, apostrophes and speech marks. They are not decoration. They tell the reader where to stop, where to pause and how to read the words.
explain: Compare «Let's eat, Grandma!» with «Let's eat Grandma!» The words are almost the same, but the comma changes the meaning completely. Punctuation can change what a sentence means, so it matters.
explain: Checking your punctuation is part of proofreading, which means hunting for small slips in spelling, punctuation and tense. Editing is different: it improves what the writing says, for example by choosing a stronger word.
fact: Punctuation is the set of marks used in writing, such as full stops, commas, question marks and apostrophes.
fact: Punctuation makes meaning clear and shows where to pause.
fact: «Check your punctuation» means look carefully at your marks to make sure they are correct.
fact: A run-on sentence joins sentences with no proper punctuation; fix it with full stops or joining words.
fact: «Eats, Shoots and Leaves» is a famous British book about punctuation.
exercise: «Let's eat, Grandma!» and «Let's eat Grandma!» differ by which mark? | A colon | An apostrophe | *A comma | A question mark
exercise: Which word is the verb related to punctuation? | *punctuate | puncture | punctuality | punctual
exercise: How can you fix a run-on sentence? | Remove all the punctuation | Make it longer with no marks | Write it all in capital letters | *Add a full stop or a joining word
test: What does proofreading hunt for? | *Small slips in spelling, punctuation and tense | Big new ideas and characters | Long words | Only the title
test: Which word is a palindrome? | Shoots | *level | Eats | Leaves
exam: How long does the grammar and punctuation paper take? | 20 minutes | *45 minutes | 60 minutes | 30 minutes
